# REQUIRES: python-api
# Programs that differ only in the cell they start from have one text and
# share the compile cache (D[cell-runtime-constants]): the values of the
# start are arguments of the entry, and the estimate of the neighbor
# capacity is rounded up to four significant bits. A start with another
# estimate hits with `Execution.neighbor_capacity`, and the capacity does
# not change the run. On the CPU, mixed and double, deterministic, at
# constant pressure with restraints (Inputs/compile_cache_cell.py).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/compile_cache_cell.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU Mixed %t | FileCheck %s
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/compile_cache_cell.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU Double %t | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: the starting cell leaves the text and the pipeline as they are, capacity 448
# CHECK-NEXT: first: compiled 1 hits 0 stored 1
# CHECK-NEXT: second: compiled 0 hits 1 stored 0
# CHECK-NEXT: second, 20 steps: same as without the cache
# CHECK-NEXT: third: capacity 416
# CHECK-NEXT: third: compiled 1 hits 0 stored 1
# CHECK-NEXT: third with the capacity of the first: compiled 0 hits 1 stored 0
# CHECK-NEXT: third, 20 steps: same with either capacity
# CHECK-NEXT: refused: Execution.neighbor_capacity must be positive, or 0 for the estimate
